      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Impostors take away control of user's ability to make sure they know how others will see them, we have very limited control of impostors and it doesn't work well on avatars that aren't basic humanoids. This choice essentially punishes anyone who wants to put in effort to make optimized avatar fallbacks that still retain some features of the full avatar so that even if the full avatar is blocked, some things like toggles or emotes can be seen across all platforms, with impostors, you're just an immersion breaking pixelated mess, at least let us upload our own impostors (fallbacks but directly attached to one specific avatar) if VRChat doesn't like having to maintain two avatar selections and wants one avatar upload to hold all the data that displays something for that avatar. The decision to remove fallback avatars in the future is absolutely not acceptable for a creative community.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
